# Cloudflare Workers local dev vars — consumed by `wrangler dev` / `opennextjs-cloudflare preview`
# Copy to `.dev.vars` and fill:
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
# Then also `cp .dev.vars .env.local` if you want `next dev` to see the same values.

# Optional: Postgres. Leave empty to use GeoJSON fallback (752件, no DB needed).
# For Workers, prefer Hyperdrive (see wrangler.jsonc) or a public Neon/Supabase URL.
# On Workers, `DATABASE_URL` is read via `process.env` (OpenNext maps `env` → `process.env`).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/db?sslmode=require"

# Example: Hyperdrive connection string is bound as `HYPERDRIVE`, not `DATABASE_URL`.
# When using Hyperdrive, set `DATABASE_URL` empty and configure `wrangler.jsonc` hyperdrive `id`.

# Cloudflare bindings (auto-populated by `wrangler types`)
# NEXT_INC_CACHE_R2_BUCKET="urbex-hunter-cache"
